WEBVTT

00:00:02.945 --> 00:00:11.852
Wealth Management
Take a discretionary mandate from the first meeting to an active, reviewed portfolio — with suitability built in.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.680
Nathalie Ramdin, an existing client, wants Genesis to manage her portfolio
Natasha, her relationship manager, opens a discretionary mandate

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:21.880
Sign in as Natasha Appadoo — Senior Relationship Manager
Senior Relationship Manager — owns the client and the mandate

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:25.360
Wealth Management ▸ Wealth Mandates: one card per mandate
Prospect ▸ Discovery ▸ Risk profiling ▸ Proposal ▸ Signed ▸ Funded ▸ Active ▸ Closed

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.760
The “Wealth mandate” button opens a two-step onboarding wizard
Client & profile, then the terms

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:35.200
No risk profile yet — she has not done the questionnaire
We leave it empty for now

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:51.360
The terms: base currency, benchmark, custodian and the portfolio manager
Review cycle and fees

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.680
Mandate created at Prospect
The agreement and the IPS are generated later from its Docs tab

00:00:54.680 --> 00:01:02.920
The discovery meeting is held — move the card on
Drag it on the board

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.760
Next: profile her risk
Move to Risk profiling and run the investor questionnaire

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.720
Wealth Management ▸ Risk Profiles: every client's profile
Each client with their score and model portfolio

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:21.200
“Investor Questionnaire” opens a three-step wizard
Done together with the client

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.640
Horizon and objectives
When will she need the money, what is she investing for

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:36.840
Attitude to risk and experience
If the portfolio fell 20% in a year, she would hold

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:44.840
Scored 55: model portfolio C — Balanced
Highest suitable product risk 3 on a 1–5 scale · valid two years, until 2028-10-17

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:50.400
Prospects can take the same questionnaire on the website
They see their profile at once, and a Wealth enquiry is created for an adviser

00:01:50.480 --> 00:02:01.720
Every recommendation is recorded with its rationale and the risks disclosed
Wealth Management ▸ Suitability Records ▸ New

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:05.560
Discretionary management is rated risk 3 — within her ceiling of 3
It saves straight away

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:18.640
She also asks about the Emerging Markets Equity Fund
Rated risk 5 — above her ceiling

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:26.320
Refused: the product is riskier than her profile allows
Above the ceiling, an override reason and the client's signed acknowledgement are required

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:30.280
Override reason recorded and the client's acknowledgement ticked
Now the recommendation can be saved — flagged as a mismatch

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:37.720
Back to the mandate: prepare the proposal (IPS)
Move it to Proposal

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:45.880
Blocked: a proposal needs the client's risk profile on the mandate
Open the record to complete it

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:58.120
Link the risk profile she just completed
The mandate takes its model portfolio from it: C

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:02.840
The IPS is agreed and the mandate signed
Agreement and IPS are signed electronically from the Docs tab

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:07.440
The client transfers her assets — Account funded
Funding is allowed only once the client's KYC is approved

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:12.480
Nathalie Ramdin's KYC is approved, so the move goes through
For a client whose KYC is still in progress, the board refuses: “Fund the account only after KYC approval.”

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:13.520
Laurent, the portfolio manager, takes over
He runs the portfolio from here

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:21.520
Sign in as Laurent Koenig — Portfolio Manager
Portfolio Manager — manages the mandate and its reviews

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:26.240
Investments are in place: the mandate becomes Active

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:39.360
Each month-end the portfolio system sends an AUM snapshot
Market value by asset class, performance and net flows

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:45.080
Amounts are in the mandate's base currency — US dollars here
Snapshots feed the mandate's performance and the net flows on the Wealth dashboard

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:54.000
The mandate's AUM is updated from the same feed
It rolls up to the client's Client 360

00:03:54.000 --> 00:04:01.440
Mandate WM-2026-000021: model portfolio, AUM in USD and MUR, YTD performance, next review
Attrition risk is watched daily: falling AUM, missed reviews or a complaint

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:11.760
Reviews follow the mandate's cycle — here quarterly
14 days before one is due, the system opens it at Scheduled; here Laurent opens one now

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:16.360
Scheduled ▸ Pack prepared ▸ Meeting held ▸ Completed
The pack is ready: the client is invited to the meeting

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:20.120
The meeting took place — move to Meeting held

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:37.760
Blocked: Meeting held needs the date it was held
Open the record to complete it

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:51.200
Record the outcome and the minutes
Completed needs both — and the client's suitability re-confirmed

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:57.520
Blocked: re-confirm the client's profile and suitability before closing the review
A rule on the Completed stage

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:08.960
Profile and suitability re-confirmed with the client

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:11.960
Review completed — the next one is due in three months
Overdue reviews show on the Wealth dashboard and the RM workbench

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:21.630
The Strategic Asset Allocation Committee changes the house view
Wealth Management ▸ SAAC Decisions ▸ New

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:28.748
Saved — every portfolio manager is notified to brief the clients in the affected models

00:05:28.788 --> 00:05:41.748
The Wealth dashboard
Active mandates, AUM, overdue reviews, attrition risk

00:05:41.748 --> 00:05:45.348
AUM by model portfolio, the mandate pipeline and net flows by month
Each widget opens the records behind it

00:05:45.348 --> 00:05:48.078
Reviews by status, suitability mismatches that were overridden, profiles by model

00:05:48.078 --> 00:05:55.788
Wealth Management
Suitability and the regulator's controls are built into every step.
